    "title": "Desirae Spearman homers twice in return to El Paso as Texas Tech sweeps UTEP - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sam Guzman No media credit provided. ,\n50 minutes ago\nEL PASO, Texas (KTSM) — Desirae Spearman is emerging as one of the top softball players to come out of El Paso.\nAfter four dominant seasons at Hanks High School, Spearman began her collegiate career in 2024 at New Mexico State in Las Cruces.\nFollowing two seasons with the Aggies, she entered the transfer portal last May and joined one of the nation’s top programs—No. 5 Texas Tech.\nOn Wednesday, April 22, Spearman returned to the Sun City as Texas Tech faced UTEP in a doubleheader.\nIn Game 1, Spearman wasted no time making an impact. In her second at-bat, she launched a no-doubt home run to center field to extend Texas Tech’s lead to 9-0 in the top of the second inning. She later added a double and another home run in the fifth inning, finishing Game 1 a perfect 3-for-3 with two home runs, a double, and a walk.\nTexas Tech rolled to a 16-0 win in the opener before completing the sweep with an 11-1 victory in Game 2.\nSpearman finished 3-for-4 with two home runs, a double, and three walks across both games.\nWhat a homecoming for Spearman.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTSM 9 News.",
